          "summary": "The agreement requires written notice of non-renewal at least 30 days before the end of the current term to prevent renewal, and 60 days' written notice for termination for convenience.",
          "findings": [
            "The agreement requires written notice of non-renewal at least 30 days before the end of the current term to prevent automatic renewal, and 60 days' written notice for a termination for convenience by the Customer.\n\n### Notice of Non-Renewal\nTo prevent the agreement from renewing for successive 12-month periods, either party must provide written notice of non-renewal.\n\n> \"The agreement renews for successive 12-month periods unless either party gives written notice of non-renewal at least 30 days before the current term ends.\"\n\n[\u00a75]\n\n### Termination for Convenience\nThe Customer may terminate the agreement for convenience by providing a specific notice period, though the Customer remains liable for subscription fees through the end of the then-current term.\n\n> \"Customer may terminate for convenience on 60 days' written notice but remains liable for subscription fees through the end of the current term.\"\n\n[\u00a76]"
          ],
